  "P0184": {"description":"Fuel Temperature Sensor A Circuit Intermittent","causes":["Loose contact or weak terminal tension in the connector","Wire break or chafing from vibration","Sensor with internal dropouts","Corrosion from moisture"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2.5 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Fuel temperature in scan data jumps; Usually no change in driving. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
