  "P018D": {"description":"Fuel Pressure Sensor B Circuit High","causes":["Sensor ground open","Signal wire shorted to 5 V or battery voltage","Sensor faulty","Connector corrosion or water ingress"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Starting problems; Lack of power; Sometimes no symptoms. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P018E": {"description":"Fuel Pressure Sensor B Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","causes":["Loose contact or connector corrosion","Chafed harness","Sensor faulty internally","CAN transmission from the pump module disturbed"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on (often intermittent); Brief stumble or hesitation; Occasional starting problems. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P018F": {"description":"Fuel System Over Pressure Relief Valve Frequent Activation","causes":["Volume control valve sticking – repeated overpressure","Rail pressure sensor reading wrong (controller targets too high)","Relief valve fatigued, opening too early","Return blocked or pressure control valve faulty","Load changes or overrun steps with software faults"],"repair":"Typical repair: hard difficulty, about 1–5 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Sudden loss of power (limp mode with low rail pressure); Starting problems once the valve no longer seals; Smoke or harsh combustion noise beforehand. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0190": {"description":"Fuel Rail Pressure Sensor A Circuit","causes":["Connector corroded or water ingress at the rail pressure sensor","Rail pressure sensor faulty","Harness damaged (heat, chafing)","5 V reference disturbed"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Limp mode, loss of power; Stalling or no start (sometimes only after a waiting time); Rough idle. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0191": {"description":"Fuel Rail Pressure Sensor A Circuit Range/Performance","causes":["Rail pressure sensor drifting or stuck (wrong offset at 0 bar)","Genuine pressure fault: high-pressure pump, pressure or volume control valve, tank pump","Connector corroded, contact resistance in signal or ground","Fuel shortage or clogged filter","Control module software"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–3 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Limp mode or 'Reduced Engine Power'; Hard starting, stalling; Rough running. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
