  "P0199": {"description":"Engine Oil Temperature Sensor A Circuit Intermittent/Erratic","causes":["Loose contact or corroded pins at the sensor connector","Harness chafing intermittently (engine movement)","Sensor with internal hairline crack","Control module ground connection"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light or only a stored code; Oil temperature reading jumps; Occasionally restricted cam timing. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
