  "P019D": {"description":"O2 Sensor Delayed Response - Lean to Rich Bank 2 Sensor 3","causes":["Sensor 3 aged, sooted or oil-poisoned","Exhaust leak ahead of sensor 3","Converter with strongly differing oxygen storage (aftermarket or new)","Sensor 3 heater weak","Control module software"],"repair":"Typical repair: easy difficulty, about 0.5–1.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; No noticeable change in driving; Catalyst readiness not set (emissions test). Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
