  "P01A8": {"description":"Alternative Fuel Rail/System Pressure - Too Low","causes":["Gas supply nearly empty, tank pressure close to the regulator minimum","High- or low-pressure shut-off valve not opening fully (coil, control, manual valve closed)","High-pressure filter or low-pressure filter/oil separator clogged","Pressure regulator faulty, sticking or iced (coolant heating disturbed)","Leak on the low-pressure side"],"repair":"Typical repair: hard difficulty, about 1–4 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Automatic switch to petrol or gas operation not possible; Loss of power or hesitation under load in gas mode; Possibly lean codes (P0171/P0174) in gas mode. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P01A9": {"description":"Alternative Fuel Rail/System Pressure - Too High","causes":["Regulator sticking or valve seat leaking (pressure creeps onto the low-pressure side)","Control of the electronically regulated regulator disturbed (PWM circuit, connector)","Rail pressure sensor reading plausible but too high (drift)","Contamination or oil in the regulator"],"repair":"Typical repair: hard difficulty, about 1–4 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Gas operation aborted or not possible, vehicle runs on petrol; Rough running or rich codes (P0172/P0175) in gas mode; Possibly gas smell (relief valve responded). Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
