  "P02FB": {"description":"Cold Start Fuel Injection Control Circuit/Open","causes":["Coil of the cold-start injector or valve open","Connector loose, corroded or pin pushed back","Broken wire in the harness","Fuse or relay of the cold-start system","Driver stage in the engine module"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Hard or no start in cold weather (especially with high ethanol); Rough running right after a cold start. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P02FC": {"description":"Cold Start Fuel Injection Control Circuit Low","causes":["Control wire chafed through, shorted to ground","Shorted turn in the cold-start injector or valve","Water or corrosion in the connector","Driver stage in the engine module"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Hard cold start, or over-fuelling with fuel smell if the valve stays open; Rough running when cold. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P02FD": {"description":"Cold Start Fuel Injection Control Circuit High","causes":["Control wire shorted to a supply wire (chafed or pinched)","Short in the cold-start injector or valve","Moisture or corrosion in the connector","Driver stage in the engine module"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Hard or no start in cold weather (especially with high ethanol). Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P02FE": {"description":"Cold Start Fuel Injection Control Circuit Range/Performance","causes":["Cold-start injector or valve worn, sticking or partly clogged","Contact resistance at connector or ground","Cold-start fuel supply faulty (auxiliary tank empty, pump, filter)","Engine module or software"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Long or failed cold start; Rough running when cold. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P02FF": {"description":"Propulsion System Inactive Timer Performance","causes":["Time source in another module (instrument cluster, body module) gives an implausible time after a reset or voltage loss","Software level of engine, transmission or instrument cluster module","Battery discharged or disconnected, voltage dips","Instrument cluster or timer in the engine module faulty","Coolant temperature sensor distorting the cooling check"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.3–2 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Check engine light on, otherwise usually nothing noticeable; Clock in the instrument cluster wrong or reset; Readiness of standstill-dependent monitors incomplete. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0300": {"description":"Random/Multiple Cylinder Misfire Detected","causes":["False air (vacuum leak, crankcase ventilation, intake gasket)","Worn or wrong spark plugs on several cylinders, faulty ignition coils","Fuel pressure too low or high, contaminated fuel","Valve timing (stretched chain), valves, compression on several cylinders","False detection: tone wheel or pulley, rough road, vibration, software"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–6 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on, flashing at a catalyst-damaging rate; Rough idle, jerking, vibration; Loss of power, hesitation; Smell of unburnt fuel, higher consumption. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0301": {"description":"Cylinder 1 Misfire Detected","causes":["Ignition coil of cylinder 1 faulty (coil, connector, ground)","Spark plug of cylinder 1 worn, sooted, cracked or wrongly gapped","Injector of cylinder 1 clogged or leaking, or its control","Low compression on cylinder 1 (valve, rings, head gasket) or local false air","Water or oil in the plug well"],"repair":"Typical repair: easy difficulty, about 0.3–4 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on, flashing at a catalyst-damaging rate; Rough idle, jerking, vibration; Loss of power, hesitation; Smell of unburnt fuel, higher consumption. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0302": {"description":"Cylinder 2 Misfire Detected","causes":["Ignition coil of cylinder 2 faulty (coil, connector, ground)","Spark plug of cylinder 2 worn, sooted, cracked or wrongly gapped","Injector of cylinder 2 clogged or leaking, or its control","Low compression on cylinder 2 (valve, rings, head gasket) or local false air","Water or oil in the plug well"],"repair":"Typical repair: easy difficulty, about 0.3–4 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on, flashing at a catalyst-damaging rate; Rough idle, jerking, vibration; Loss of power, hesitation; Smell of unburnt fuel, higher consumption. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
