  "P0362": {"description":"Ignition Coil L Primary Control Circuit/Open","causes":["Ignition coil L faulty (output stage in the coil or primary winding open)","Connector at the coil corroded, wet or with a loose pin","Control, supply or ground wire open or chafed","Driver in the engine module faulty or software (permanent dwell)"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Misfire and rough running on cylinder 12, often also P0312; Loss of power, jerking under load; Cylinder shut off (injection off), risk to the catalyst if driven on. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0363": {"description":"Misfire Detected - Fueling Disabled","causes":["Ignition coil or spark plug of the affected cylinder faulty","Injector sticking or leaking, or fuel pressure too low","Engine module software (misfire detection, cold-start mixture)","Mechanical cause: loss of compression, valve or carbon deposits, vacuum leak"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–4 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Check engine light on steadily instead of flashing; Clearly rough running, one cylinder without power; Loss of power; Jerking or stalling, especially when cold. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0364": {"description":"DC/AC Converter Control Module Control Circuit Range/Performance","causes":["Control or enable line to the converter module disturbed (connector, wiring)","Converter control module faulty internally","Software of the modules involved"],"repair":"Typical repair: hard difficulty, about 1–4 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Warning lamp depending on the manufacturer; Converter function restricted (for example power socket or hybrid drive). Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0365": {"description":"Camshaft Position Sensor B Circuit Bank 1","causes":["Exhaust camshaft position sensor faulty","Connector or wiring open or corroded, 5 V reference missing","Oil in the connector from a leaking sensor O-ring","Tone wheel on the exhaust phaser damaged or loose","Engine module (5 V supply)"],"repair":"Typical repair: easy difficulty, about 0.3–1 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Longer cranking before the engine starts; Loss of power or rough idle (exhaust cam timing in its base position); Higher fuel consumption. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0366": {"description":"Camshaft Position Sensor B Circuit Range/Performance Bank 1","causes":["Sensor faulty or dirty (metal debris on the magnet)","Wiring close to ignition coils or solenoids, loose contact","Tone wheel on the phaser damaged or loose, air gap too large","Sensor or phaser wrongly fitted after timing drive work"],"repair":"Typical repair: easy difficulty, about 0.3–1.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Longer cranking before the engine starts; Loss of power or rough idle (exhaust cam timing in its base position); Higher fuel consumption. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
