  "P0368": {"description":"Camshaft Position Sensor B Circuit High Bank 1","causes":["Connector off or corroded, signal wire open","5 V reference or ground of the sensor open","Sensor faulty (output does not switch)","Signal wire shorted to positive"],"repair":"Typical repair: easy difficulty, about 0.3–1.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Longer cranking before the engine starts; Loss of power or rough idle (exhaust cam timing in its base position). Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0369": {"description":"Camshaft Position Sensor B Circuit Intermittent Bank 1","causes":["Loose contact in connector or wiring","Interference from the ignition (routing, shielding)","Sensor with metal debris or borderline air gap","Tone wheel or phaser damaged"],"repair":"Typical repair: easy difficulty, about 0.3–1.5 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Sporadic jerking or stalling; Occasional starting problems. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
