  "P0389": {"description":"Crankshaft Position Sensor B Circuit Intermittent","causes":["Loose contact or corrosion at the sensor B connector","Wire break or chafing that appears with engine movement","Electrical interference (add-on devices, routing near ignition or relays)","Tone wheel damaged or dirty, air gap too large","Sensor faulty, temperature-dependent"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–3 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on, possibly only after several trips; Occasional stalling or jerking; Sporadic starting problems. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
