  "P0390": {"description":"Camshaft Position Sensor B Circuit Bank 2","causes":["Connector or wiring of the bank 2 exhaust sensor open or corroded (signal, 5 V, ground)","Camshaft position sensor faulty","Oil contamination or leak at the sensor, sensor loose","Tone wheel on the phaser damaged or wrongly fitted after timing chain work","Engine module, or 5 V reference shorted by another sensor"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–2 h, often DIY. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Loss of power (bank 2 exhaust cam timing in its base position); Longer cranking; Rough idle; Higher fuel consumption. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
