  "P0395": {"description":"Cylinder 1 Pressure Sensor Circuit","causes":["Connector at the pressure-sensing glow plug loose or corroded","Reference, signal or ground wire open or shorted","Sensor electronics in the glow plug faulty","Engine module (reference voltage or input)"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 0.5–3 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Check engine light on (often after two trips); Usually barely noticeable – combustion control for the cylinder is switched off; Possibly rougher running, more noise or slightly higher consumption. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
  "P0396": {"description":"Cylinder 1 Pressure Sensor Circuit Range/Performance","causes":["Sensor in the glow plug drifting (deposits, ageing)","Glow plug leaking or wrongly torqued (pressure transmitted wrongly)","Contact resistance in connector or ground","Actual compression pressure differs (valve, rings)"],"repair":"Typical repair: medium difficulty, about 1–3 h, usually a shop job. Symptoms: Check engine light on; Combustion control for the cylinder off – slightly rough running, more noise; Possibly more smoke or consumption. Confirm with the factory service manual before replacing parts."},
